Spec: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/spec.md (gateway dump; AC54, AC55, AC56, AC57)
Research: Q7 (decode limit is capture.max_body_bytes), Q9 (mode=ro may create -wal/-shm; dump never writes gateway.db or a blob)
Why this approach: run hands args[0] == "dump" to runDump before its own flag parsing; both share loadConfig and captureDir (extracted from run), so dump finds the store through the same sources. store.OpenReader checks gateway.db exists first, so a fresh or missing directory is never touched. Output is built in a bytes.Buffer and written once, so a read error part-way prints only the failure line. Details recorded in plan.md ("Details fixed in T25").
Alternatives rejected: a bufio.Writer streaming output (every write needs an unchecked-error dance and a partial dump on error); logging the typed request ID on "exchange not found" (001 never logs positional arguments).
Trade-off / known limit: the whole output is held in memory (bounded by two bodies at max_body_bytes plus events). capture.enabled is ignored by dump. Failure lines go to stdout as JSON log lines, like every other gateway line. -raw prints encoded bytes as they are, binary included.
Verified by: TestDump_PrintsExchange (streamed, non_streamed, gzip, br, zstd, raw_flag, unsupported_encoding; exact full-output comparison), TestDump_Last (-last and --last), TestDump_UnknownIDFails (unknown_id, missing_store), TestDump_NeverWritesStore (fresh_dir, gateway_stopped, gateway_running; gateway.db and blob size+mtime unchanged), TestDump_BadArguments, make verify. All failed against a stubbed runDump except fresh_dir; mutation (dump opening store.Open first) failed fresh_dir and missing_store.
